{"parentUuid":"385c3d93-5777-4d62-872f-5aea96d0f8ad","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a69dc108738e5f780","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf4TLwwQwaWLthrrg7vsf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1526,"cache_read_input_tokens":238249,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1526,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cf4TLvrBcLiLN3SyfMGZm","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"9dd83686-f3d1-4c7f-998c-d279181a98fc","timestamp":"2026-09-15T02:42:41.562Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"df3b3576-b317-408d-964a-187d57ed18ca","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"9dd83686-f3d1-4c7f-998c-d279181a98fc","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a69dc108738e5f780","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf4TLwwQwaWLthrrg7vsf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014dAqXH7UruwgGe18qE5Lpu","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"I built the calendar file: 65 two-hour project blocks, none skipped, 3 moved off their preferred weekday. The whole test suite passes. Nothing was committed, portfolio.json is untouched and no calendar events were changed.\n\n**Calendar file:** `/Users/kristinarash/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-eric.rash11@gmail.com/My Drive/00_Primary_Storage_Drive/05_SYSTEMS/ProjectBlocks/fall-2026-project-blocks.ics`\n\n**Test result:** `Ran 240 tests in 19.420s — OK`. That includes 19 new tests in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage/tests/test_slate_calendar.py`.\n\n**Code:** `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage/slate_calendar.py`. It has `plan_blocks` and `to_ics` plus the CLI.\n\n**Calendar snapshot:** `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/df3b3576/tmp/work-calendar-busy.json`, 200 events.\n\n**File checks:**\n- 65 events, each with a unique ID.\n- Lines use CRLF endings and none is longer than 75 bytes.\n- I re-read the first 2 events and they are correct.\n- Times convert to UTC correctly on both sides of the Nov 1 clock change (10/30 08:00 → 13:00Z, 11/6 08:00 → 14:00Z).\n\n**First 2 weeks**\n| Date | Time | Project |\n|---|---|---|\n| Tue 9/15 | 08:30–10:30 | HPI protocol (Focus time) |\n| Tue 9/15 | 14:00–16:00 | Tech Inventory (moved) |\n| Wed 9/16 | 09:30–11:30 | Education curriculum |\n| Thu 9/17 | 14:00–16:00 | Return to Performance course |\n| Fri 9/18 | 07:00–09:00 | Women's health survey (Focus time) |\n| Mon 9/21 | 08:00–10:00 | Tech Inventory (Focus time) |\n| Tue 9/22 | 08:30–10:30 | HPI protocol (Focus time) |\n| Wed 9/23 | 08:00–10:00 | Education curriculum (Focus time) |\n| Thu 9/24 | 13:00–15:00 | Return to Performance course (Focus time) |\n| Fri 9/25 | 08:00–10:00 | Women's health survey (Focus time) |\n\nWeek 1 skips two Focus time slots because a meeting sits inside them: Power Hour on Wed 9/16 and Eric/Craig on Thu 9/17.\n\nIn later weeks, Wednesday moves to 09:30 on 10/14 and 11/11 because of Power Hour. Thursday settles at 13:00, since 10:30 would run into lunch.\n\n**Moved blocks**\n- **Tech Inventory, Mon 9/14 → Tue 9/15 14:00:** Monday is already past. HPI keeps Tuesday's Focus time, and the earlier open times hit lunch or Care Team.\n- **Return to Performance course, Thu 11/26 → Mon 11/23 13:00:** Thanksgiving.\n- **Women's health survey, Fri 11/27 → Tue 11/24 14:00:** Thanksgiving. Monday had no second free 2-hour window.\n\n**Assumptions**\n1. Each week, blocks go on their preferred day first. A moved block only gets what's left and never takes another project's preferred slot.\n2. The 07:30 earliest start only applies when scanning for free time. A Focus time slot that starts at 07:00 (Fri 9/18) is used as is.\n3. Events with no title count as busy. \"Power Hour \" (with a trailing space) is busy too; only events titled exactly \"Focus time\" count as free.\n4. Each event ID includes the date the block landed on. If a later rerun moves a block to a different day, the new copy gets a new ID. The old event stays in the calendar until deleted by hand. Keying IDs to the week instead would avoid that; that's Eric's call.\n5. I added a DTSTAMP timestamp to each event. The calendar file standard requires it and Outlook rejects files without it.\n6. Python 3.9 compatibility was checked by parsing both files with 3.9 grammar only. There is no 3.9 interpreter on this machine.\n\nWeeks after 9/25 were planned against recurring meetings only, because Focus time isn't booked that far out yet. Rerunning in about 2 weeks will re-fit them, and the CLI starts from tomorrow by default."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"u